course: dictionary
lesson: 9993
title: Teen and -teen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Teen is a short word for teenager. A teenager is a person aged 13 to 19, so teen means the same thing. You can see it in «a teen magazine», which is a magazine written for teenagers, and in the phrase «in her teens», which means she is between 13 and 19.
explain: The ending -teen is different. It is found at the end of the numbers 13 to 19, and it means "and ten". Thirteen is ten plus three, fourteen is ten plus four, and so on. The clue to hearing the difference is stress: in thirteen the loud beat is on -teen, but in thirty it is on the first part, THIR-ty.
explain: Context helps you spot which meaning is used. «Feet grow fast in childhood, and usually stop growing in the early to mid teens» is about ages, so teens means teenage years. «By his teens he had a ringing in his ears» tells you the boy had the problem by the time he was a teenager.
fact: A teen is a teenager, a person aged 13 to 19.
fact: «In her teens» means aged between 13 and 19.
fact: The ending -teen is found in the numbers 13 to 19 and means "and ten".
fact: «Thirteen» has its stress on -TEEN, but «thirty» has its stress on THIR-, so listen for the beat to tell them apart.
fact: «Children usually grow about 5 to 6 centimetres a year, faster as babies and again during the teenage years.»
exercise: «Feet grow fast in childhood, and usually stop growing in the early to mid teens.» What does teens mean here? | Shoes and socks | Numbers from 1 to 9 | *Ages 13 to 19 | The last days of the school year
exercise: In maths, thirteen is ten plus three. Which number is thirteen? | 3 | 31 | *13 | 30
exercise: Which phrase means aged between 13 and 19? | Teen magazine | Thirty-one | *In her teens | Early bird
test: What does teen mean in «a teen magazine»? | Very old | Made of wood | Very loud | *For teenagers
test: Which number ends in -teen? | Sixty | *Fifteen | Twelve | Twenty
exam: Ella says thirteen and thirty sound the same. Which number is ten plus three? | Thirty-three | Thirty | Three | *Thirteen
